= Mikhail Borodin

A long-serving Communist agent and advisor, Mikhail Borodin had served in a number of roles within and without the Soviet Government until being sent to assist the Kuomintang in 1923. Since then, he has become an integral piece of the Nationalist Government, and much of our organizational structure and revolutionary vigor can be owed to him. 

